WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.023
- [Instructor] In this video,

00:00:01.023 --> 00:00:02.980
we're going to further build our intuition

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.030
for multiplying decimals.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.100
So let's say that we wanted to figure out

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.640
what eight times seven tenths is.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.550
Pause this video and see if you can figure

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.243
this out on your own.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.130
All right, now there's several ways

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:21.400
that we could approach what
eight times seven tenths is.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.830
We could view this as eight times,

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:27.240
and we could write seven
tenths as a fraction.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.360
So we can re-express this as seven tenths,

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.810
seven over 10 is the same thing as 0.7.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.590
And we already know how
to multiply fractions,

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.140
you could view this as being equal to,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.070
eight is the same thing as
eight over one or eight wholes,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:48.400
I guess you could say,
times seven over 10,

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.290
times seven tenths, which
is going to be equal to,

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:56.400
if we multiply our numerator,
we're going to get 56.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.080
And if we multiply our
denominators, we get tenths.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.110
And that makes sense.

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:04.870
If I have eight times seven
tenths, I end up with 56 tenths.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.600
Now 56 tenths can also be written as,

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.560
this is the same thing
as 50, plus six over 10,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:18.560
which is the same thing as
50 over 10, plus six over 10.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:22.670
And so this is the same thing
as, this is five wholes,

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:26.860
so five and six tenths,
five and six tenths,

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:31.223
which we can write as five
and six tenths, or 5.6.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:35.070
And it's always good to do a
little bit of a reality check,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:38.290
whenever you get an answer when
you're multiplying decimals.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.970
Say, okay, seven tenths is
a little bit less than one.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.330
So we would expect this product,

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:44.810
if we're multiplying eight times something

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.470
a little bit less than one,

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:47.650
we would expect the product to be

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:49.220
a little bit less than eight.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.040
So 5.6 makes sense.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.440
If for some reason we got,

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.480
the we you computed something
and you were to get 60,

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:56.680
you say, well, that doesn't make sense,

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.160
I should get a value less than eight.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.710
And similarly, if you somehow got a value

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:02.780
or product of like one, you're like, well,

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:05.030
that's a lot less than
eight, I should get something

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.970
that is seven tenths of eight.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:10.180
Now, another way that
you could approach this

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:14.300
is you could view this as the
same thing as eight times,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.690
and once again, I'm just gonna write this

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.913
in a different way, eight times seven,

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.830
eight times seven tenths.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:24.840
So, if you have eight
times seven of something,

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.650
what is that going to be equal to?

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:29.510
Well, eight times seven, that's 56.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:30.343
So you're going to be,

00:02:30.343 --> 00:02:34.112
this is going to be equal to 56 tenths,

00:02:34.112 --> 00:02:36.850
56 tenths.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:39.760
And one way to think about 56 tenths,

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.760
56 tenths is the same thing as 50 tenths,

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.930
50, let me color code that differently.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:51.690
So this is going to be the
same thing as 50 tenths,

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:55.700
50 tenths, plus six tenths,

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:00.700
plus the six tenths, get
right tenths, six tenths,

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.190
and 50 tenths is the
same thing as five ones.

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:09.710
So five ones, and six tenths,

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.690
which is exactly what we have here,

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.770
five ones, and six tenths.

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:17.080
Let's do another example,

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.560
that's a little bit more involved.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:24.560
So let's say that we want to figure out,

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.860
we want to figure out what is

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:31.773
three times 0.87.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:36.333
Pause this video and
try to figure that out.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.360
Well, once again, there's
many ways to approach it.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.310
But we could just start with
the way that we just looked at.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:47.210
We could say, hey, this is
the same thing as three times,

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:49.510
and we can re-express this as,

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:52.300
this is the same thing as 87 hundredths.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.423
87 hundredths,

00:03:56.380 --> 00:04:01.090
and so if I have three
times 87 of something,

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:02.600
what am I going to be left with?

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:03.650
Well, this is going to be equal

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.620
to some number of hundredths,

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.550
and to figure out that, we just figure out

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.190
what's three times 87?

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:12.270
So 87 times three,

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.200
seven times three is 21,

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.000
we regroup that two, becomes two 10s.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.450
And then eight times three is 24.

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.140
And that's really 24 10s
plus those other two 10s,

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:29.140
so we get 26 10s, which is
the same thing as 206 10s,

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.540
but it's gonna be 261.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:34.910
So the three times 87 of
something is going to be 261

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:38.600
of that something, and this
case something is hundredths.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:42.800
So this is 261 hundredths.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.600
So how do we express this as a decimal?

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.820
Well, there's a couple of
ways that you can approach it.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.240
You can think about is
this is the ones place,

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.200
this is the tenths place,
this is the hundredths place.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.920
And so very clearly, 100th here

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.020
would be one in the hundredths place.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:06.020
If you have 60 hundredths, which
is what the six represents,

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:11.080
60 hundredths is the
same thing as six tenths.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:15.843
And then last but not least,
if you have 200 hundredths,

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.300
that's the same thing as two wholes.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.930
Another way to think about it is,

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.520
you go to the hundredths place,

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.040
and then you start from
there, but you write out 261,

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:30.070
one, the 60 hundredths, and
then the 200 hundredths,

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:33.080
and you get 2.61.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:35.250
Now another way that you
could have approached this,

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.740
and we saw this in the last example,

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.340
is you could say hey, this
is going to be the same thing

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:44.340
as three times at 87 hundredths.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:45.530
(mumbles) These are all equivalent,

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:46.510
but hopefully one of these,

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:47.840
or more than one of these register

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:49.830
with you of what's really going on.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:53.960
Well, this is going to be the
same thing as three wholes,

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:57.880
times 87 hundredths, 87 hundredths.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.740
And so this is going to be
equal to, in the numerator,

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.660
we have three times 87.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:08.660
Three times 87 hundredths,
one times 100 is 100.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.000
Three times 87 hundredths,
well, we already know

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:16.000
what three times 87 is, this
is equal to 261 hundredths.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:20.610
And you can see 100
goes into 261, two times

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:23.850
and you're left with 61 hundredths.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:26.780
So these are all
equivalent representations.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.840
And just reminder, so it's
always good to estimate.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:32.240
And so what you have is you
have three times something

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.200
that's a little bit less than one.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.710
So you would expect a value,
a little bit less than three.

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:40.550
And so 2.61 also meets that sniff test,

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:41.530
that this seems about right.

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:44.620
If for some reason you got 26 or 261,

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:48.750
that would be way off or
even if you got 0.261,

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.900
that would also feel way off.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.483
So hopefully this is helpful.

